; The word at CODE:0294 is a variable the entry code writes (it differs from
; the file in a run's memory dump), not an instruction. Presumably the call
; before it at CODE:0291 does not return and the next routine begins with the
; PUSH BP at CODE:0298; no run executed 0291 or 0298 (not checked further).
stop CODE:0291
code CODE:0298

; First instruction starts observed outside decoded code in runs that leave the
; intro with Esc (at 5, 40, 125, 200 and 300 s; some with other keys and mouse
; buttons before).
code CODE:02CC
code CODE:2AB2
code S02AF:0001

; Jump tables read from the generated source (not seen taken entry by entry):
; the bounded parser dispatch through CODE:0D0E (CMP BX,17H), a switch by
; value with seven values at S056A:146D and their targets after them, the two
; 16-entry dispatches on a byte's upper four bits in S071F, and in S0C57 two
; bounded tables (CMP BX,6) and three switches by value (5, 4 and 4 values).
words CODE:0D0E 18 CODE
words S056A:147B 7 S056A
words S071F:1749 10 S071F
words S071F:1917 10 S071F
words S0C57:0CC1 5 S0C57
words S0C57:0CAF 4 S0C57
words S0C57:0C99 7 S0C57
words S0C57:0C91 4 S0C57
words S0C57:0C7B 7 S0C57

